ell as a two-fold  increased risk of developing a chronic  disease and a 20 to 98 percent increase  in all major risk factors so to  summarize that belonging to an ethnic  group and having an increased risk of  developing diabetes is not a you problem  and it has nothing to do with the nature  of your ethnic background instead it's a  complex systemic issue that increases  health disparities in these groups and  puts them at a disadvantage for  developing chronic disease a great  example of this is the healthy immigrant  effect where the health status of  immigrants tend to decline the longer  they remain in their host country due to  environmental factors and lack of access  to health services so to summarize can  you prevent diabetes from progressing  into diabetes yes absolutely you can the  goal is to focus on health behaviors  that not only improve insulin  sensitivity but can also help to lower  stress on the body so this includes  regular physical activity that you  actually enjoy especially aerobic and  resistance exercises and including a  balance of macros that combine carbs  into hunger crushing combos i told you  there was a lot a lot to cover but if  you have questions leave them below and  i can follow up with another video if  you'd like so on that note that is all  that i have for you guys today if you  like this video be sure to give it the  thumbs up leave me a comment below again  any questions that you have subscribe to  the channel and i'll see you next time  on abby's kitchen bye  [Music]
 

